        "original_id": "70306dee-91e5-504a-91f4-f7ec4ec872b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Prince, Space Cowboy, Dywane Thomas Jr.\n- Groups: The Revolution\n- Works: \"I Would Die 4 U\", Purple Rain, Purple Rain (film)\n- Topics: album sales, cover versions\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Prince released Purple Rain as his sixth studio album, the first to feature The Revolution, and as the soundtrack to the film Purple Rain.\n- In 1984, \"I Would Die 4 U\" was released by Prince and The Revolution as the fourth US single from the album Purple Rain.\n- Purple Rain has sold over 25 million copies worldwide, making it the third-best-selling soundtrack album of all time.\n- In 2002, Space Cowboy adopted that stage name and recorded a cover of Prince's song \"I Would Die 4 U.\"\n- Dywane Thomas Jr. is known for his bass guitar performances on YouTube and for being one of the last people to work with Prince.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a794ba11-3d03-5e1f-82e7-2f368b89e523",
        "text": "Page: I Would Die 4 U. Sentence: \"I Would Die 4 U\" is a song by Prince and The Revolution, and the fourth single in the US from their 1984 album, \"Purple Rain\".\nPage: Purple Rain (album). Sentence: Purple Rain is the sixth studio album by American recording artist Prince, the first to feature his band The Revolution, and is the soundtrack to the 1984 film of the same name.\nPage: Purple Rain (album). Sentence: To date, it has sold over 25 million copies worldwide, making it the third-best-selling soundtrack album of all time.\nPage: Space Cowboy (musician). Sentence: In 2002, Dresti changed his stage name to Space Cowboy and did a cover of Prince's song, \"I Would Die 4 U.\"\nPage: Dywane Thomas Jr.. Sentence: He is known for his presence on YouTube playing bass guitar and known for being one of the last people to work with Prince.",
